  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l05_recent_replay_sampling(game_records: list, window_size: int = 100, batch_size: int = 4, seed: int = 42) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract training samples from a sliding window of recent self-play games, maintaining a deterministic random sampling procedure to feed dual-head neural network training batches.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nExtract training samples from a sliding window of recent self-play games, maintaining a deterministic random sampling procedure to feed dual-head neural network training batches.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l05_recent_replay_sampling(game_records: list, window_size: int = 100, batch_size: int = 4, seed: int = 42) -> list:\n    all_pos = [pos for g in game_records for pos in g.get('positions', [])]\n    recent = all_pos[-window_size:] if len(all_pos) > window_size else all_pos\n    if not recent: return []\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    indices = sorted(rng.choice(len(recent), size=min(batch_size, len(recent)), replace=False))\n    return [recent[i] for i in indices]\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
